Sync Unit examples
==================

ethercat-conf.xml splits one 1 ms EtherCAT master into two process-data
domains:

- "slow" is exchanged every 2 ms.
- "fast" is exchanged every 1 ms.

multirate-conf.xml with multirate.hal runs an 8 kHz bus and services each
slower Sync Unit from a HAL thread of its own rate:

- the default unit (an EL3162 analog input) at 8 kHz in ecat-thread,
- "motion" (a DC drive) at 2 kHz in servo-thread,
- "io" (an EL1809) at 1 kHz in io-thread, exchanged on the third
  master cycle of each millisecond (syncUnitPhase="2"),
- "serial" at 250 Hz, left to ecat-thread.

All slaves sharing a syncUnit name must specify the same syncUnitCycle and
syncUnitPhase. If the attributes are omitted, the slave uses the default
Sync Unit at the master rate. See documentation/multi-rate.md for a
walkthrough and documentation/distributed-clocks.md for the reference.

Replace the placeholder slave types and IDs with the actual devices and PDO
mappings.
